@squinch/pack-gcp
=================

This package redistributes Google Cloud's product icons.

Icon assets (icons/*.svg)
-------------------------
Copyright Google LLC. All rights reserved.

Source:  https://cloud.google.com/icons
Release: 2026-05 (the "Updated" date on Google's product-icons PDF, the only
         version marker the library publishes)

The footing this pack ships on, stated plainly
----------------------------------------------
Google publishes NO redistribution grant for these icons. The icon library
page says, in full, what they are for:

  Welcome to the official library for Google Cloud product icons. Here you
  can find the Google Cloud product icons you need for your diagrams,
  technical documentation, and more.

The ZIPs carry no licence file and the PDF that accompanies them carries no
terms. That is less than Microsoft gives Azure's icons ("you can copy,
distribute, and display the icons" for architecture diagrams) and much less
than the CC0, ISC and Apache-2.0 grants behind the other packs.

This pack relies on two things instead: Google's stated purpose for the
library — architecture diagrams and technical documentation, which is exactly
what Squinch draws — and long-standing practice. draw.io, the `diagrams`
Python package on PyPI, Iconify, IcePanel's gcpicons.com and several PlantUML
sprite libraries have redistributed these icons for years, openly, with no
objection from Google that we could find. If Google objects, this pack will be
withdrawn. Consumers of it acquire no more rights than we have: use the
artwork for Google Cloud architecture diagrams and documentation, nothing
else.

The files are Google's, byte for byte
-------------------------------------
Nothing here is recoloured, reshaped, run through an optimizer or stripped of
metadata. Regenerate this directory with `npm run fetch`, never by hand; the
fetch pins each of Google's ZIPs by content hash and refuses to run on
artwork nobody reviewed. The one treatment the files need in order to render
happens at load time in @squinch/core, not in the files: Google's export puts
the paint of sixteen icons in a `<style>` element as class rules, which the
load-time sanitizer moves onto the shapes as presentation attributes. Values
are moved verbatim, never altered. Theme treatment (placement, clipping,
plates) is likewise render-time only.

What is in here, and what is not
--------------------------------
Google replaced its product iconography in early 2025. The current system,
which is what this pack ships, is 19 unique icons for core products (4-colour)
and 26 category icons (2-colour); every other product is drawn with its
category's icon, by Google's design. pack.json encodes that: the products
named in Google's category tables resolve, as aliases, to the category glyph
Google says to draw them with.

The 216 "legacy console icons" — the per-service two-tone blue set most
third-party mirrors carry — are deliberately absent. Google's PDF says of
them: "these icons should not be used as of 2026."

